submission.summary:
Milestone 1 submitted: work/rational-hitting/worker-karn @ ac19679 = 65f2ccd + a clean merge of current origin/main (Space/Savitch files only, disjoint from this scope). All six gates passed on 65f2ccd (scripts/check.sh, 33 min); a rerun on ac19679 is in progress and I will note its result. git diff --check is clean; 26 files changed, +7859/-1.
RESULT (namespace Cslib.Circuits.Rational; entry Circuit/Rational.lean plus 22 modules under Circuit/Rational/):
- Native formula: Rational.Formula n := Circuits.Formula ratSignature n (abbrev); RatOp const q/add/mul/inv; reducible ratSignature; constructor abbrevs var/const/add/mul/inv; five-case Formula.inductionOn; nodeCount = size + leafSize (the source node measure). No second inductive, no bridge.
- Formula.Eval: relational over any Ring with c : Q ->+* R, defined by structural recursion; inv requires an actual two-sided inverse.
- Formula.evalMatrix?: native Formula.eval under an Option-valued matrixInterpretation (det != 0 -> det^-1 * adjugate); exact evalMatrix?_eq_some_iff.
ENDPOINTS:
- hittingList (computable).
- hittingList_hits for ALL s: positive-parameter Generator.list_hits plus the new hits_zero : Hits 0 H.
- hittingList_dimension_le: dimension <= 256(n+s+1)^10.
- hittingList_encoding_length_le for ALL n: <= outputConstant (n+s+1)^104. polynomial_H was re-proved without 1 <= n, so its coefficient rises from 24577 to 49153 and outputConstant grows; this is documented and pinned in the tests.
- admissible_inv_iff_nonzero and Admissible.exists_dimension_le.
- Formula.admissible?/nonzero? with _eq_true_iff (admissibility uses Hits (s+2), nonzeroness uses Hits s), and computable Decidable instances.
Positive dimension is retained everywhere. No polynomial bit-complexity claim for evaluation; the polynomial-time generator is future work and the TM0/stack chain is excluded.
COLLAPSES: Matrix.det_le; Nat.lt_two_pow_self / Nat.one_le_pow; totalDegree_list_prod + List.sum_le_length_nsmul; Submodule.equivMapOfInjective; HahnSeries.ofPowerSeries range for integrality; LinearEquiv.funCongrLeft Fin.revPerm; AddChar.sum_mulShift; Batteries Vector.get_ofFn. One scoped HahnSeries CharZero instance replaces three copies. Exponents unified. The duplicate Internal API was merged (Detection folded into MatrixEval). About 200 lines of dead v1 code removed. Mathlib.Tactic is no longer re-exported.
TESTS (ComplexityTests/RationalHitting.lean):
- concrete formulas and their nodeCount; generic DecidableEq;
- a genuine two-sided inverse in Q and on 2x2 matrices;
- Nonzero/Admissible witnesses, including the commutator (nonzero on 2x2, vanishing on 1x1); non-admissible inverses;
- s = 0 and n = 0 boundaries; dimension values by kernel decide;
- executable runs of the staged determinant, Parameters at n = s = 0, atPoint, the generator on small grids, and admissibilityTest/nonzeroTest on hand-built lists;
- 9 #print axioms guards, all [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].
SOURCE CREDIT: v1 Authors lines kept (OpenAI on core ports; Samuel Schlesinger on MatrixEval/Defs and MatrixEval; both on the entry file). Every module cites [OpenAI2026RationalHitting] @adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a and [Schlesinger2026RationalHitting] @add0aca8ee0d71e68969f2cb45cf91554a50f787.
CONTRIBUTORS (AI-assisted; none of this is human approval):
- worker-karn, a Claude Code agent run for GitHub user karnseth;
- its implementation subagents, each in its own worktree with its own cache: formula-refactor, math-a, math-b, boundary+tests, collapse, review-fix;
- read-only mapping and self-review subagents;
- worker-inference's probe, adapted for RatOp/ratSignature, the Index/Fintype/DecidableEq recursion, inductionOn and Formula.decidableEq. worker-inference is therefore not independent for those parts.
The test file's header says Samuel Schlesinger per repo convention; please confirm or name the intended author.
